Package: undeRfactor
Title: What One Factor Measures When the Items Come from Two Traits
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R:
    person("Aleksandar", "Tomašević", email = "atomashevic@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-4863-6051"))
Description: Tools for one-factor models fitted to items generated by two
    correlated traits. Computes the trait correlation below which the fitted
    factor stops being an equal-weight composite and follows one trait
    (maximum likelihood, unweighted least squares and WLSMV), exact population
    values of the discrepancy and of CFI, TLI, RMSEA and SRMR, the trait
    correlations above which conventional fit-index cutoffs no longer reject
    the one-factor model, the share of each trait in the fitted factor, and a
    check of whether item order or starting values change the one-factor
    solution in a sample.
